<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Grant returns two weeks after his first visit, on the afternoon of his otolaryngology consultation. This morning the otolaryngologist examined him with a flexible laryngoscope, which showed an ulcerated lesion of the right tonsillar pillar with a clear larynx, and took a biopsy. The pathologist&apos;s same-day frozen section shows squamous cell carcinoma; p16 staining and the final report will follow within a few days. Last week&apos;s contrast CT of the neck showed a right tonsillar mass with one enlarged right level II lymph node. His throat pain is unchanged at 5 of 10. He takes the acetaminophen solution two or three times a day and uses the lidocaine rinse when the pain is worst. He manages soft foods and liquids and has lost 1 kg in two weeks. He smoked his last cigar a week ago, on the quit date set at his first visit, and has not smoked since. Varenicline taken without food made him queasy, so he stayed on 0.5 mg twice daily for an extra week; taken after meals it no longer causes nausea. He has noticed no change in mood, sleep, or dreams. He wants a treatment plan quickly so that he can keep working on his memoir. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Workup today</td><td>Flexible laryngoscopy and biopsy; frozen section shows squamous cell carcinoma, p16 and final report pending</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Contrast CT of the neck last week: right tonsillar mass and one enlarged right level II node</td></tr><tr><td>Pain</td><td>5 of 10, unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>Swallowing and weight</td><td>Soft foods and liquids; down 1 kg in two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>No cigars for one week, since the agreed quit date</td></tr><tr><td>Varenicline tolerance</td><td>Nausea only when taken without food; no mood or sleep change</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

