<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Squamous cell carcinoma of the right tonsillar pillar, staging in progress (C09.1)</content>. The frozen section from this morning&apos;s biopsy shows squamous cell carcinoma. The CT shows a right tonsillar primary with one enlarged right level II node. The p16 status and the stage are not yet known. [S]<list><item>PET/CT for staging next week, as ordered at the first visit.</item><item>Referral to the multidisciplinary head and neck oncology team as soon as the final pathology is reported.</item><item>Dental evaluation and a speech-language pathology swallowing baseline once the treatment plan is known, before any radiation.</item><item>Primary care review after staging.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Nicotine dependence, cigars, one week abstinent (F17.290)</content>. Abstinent since the agreed quit date a week ago. Varenicline is tolerated when taken after meals. [S]<list><item>Increase varenicline to 1 mg twice daily after meals.</item><item>Brief counseling today: stopping now improves treatment results and healing; remove the remaining cigars from the house.</item><item>A 12-week course, with a further 12 weeks if he stays abstinent, to prevent relapse.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Oropharyngeal dysphagia from the tonsillar tumor (R13.12)</content>. Pain 5 of 10, unchanged; swallowing soft foods and liquids safely. [S]<list><item>Continue the acetaminophen solution, no more than 3,000 mg a day, and the lidocaine rinse.</item><item>Wait 60 minutes after the lidocaine rinse before eating or drinking.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Unintended weight loss (R63.4)</content>. Weight 77 kg, down 1 kg (1.3 percent) from 78 kg at intake. [S]<list><item>Dietitian referral now, before treatment.</item><item>Soft, calorie-dense diet with two oral supplement drinks a day; weight at every visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Head and neck examination with flexible laryngoscopy</td><td>At diagnosis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Done by the otolaryngologist this morning: ulcerated right tonsillar pillar lesion; larynx clear</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Biopsy with pathology and p16 immunohistochemistry</td><td>At diagnosis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Biopsy taken this morning. The frozen section shows squamous cell carcinoma; p16 and the final report are pending</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Contrast-enhanced CT of the neck</td><td>At diagnosis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Done last week: right tonsillar mass with one enlarged right level II node</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>PET/CT for staging</td><td>Once carcinoma is confirmed</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Booked for next week</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Otolaryngology–head and neck surgery</td><td>Urgently, within two weeks of presentation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen today, two weeks after presentation</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Multidisciplinary head and neck oncology team</td><td>After tissue diagnosis</td><td>Due</td><td>Referral to follow the final pathology report within days</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Dental evaluation before radiation</td><td>Before radiation to the neck</td><td>Due</td><td>To be booked once the treatment plan is known</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Speech-language pathology swallowing baseline</td><td>Before treatment</td><td>Due</td><td>To be booked with the dental evaluation</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Dietitian assessment</td><td>Before treatment</td><td>Referred</td><td>Referred today because of painful swallowing and a 1 kg weight loss</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>77 kg, down 1 kg (1.3 percent) from intake</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Throat pain score (0-10)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>5 of 10, unchanged from intake</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-2)</td><td>Every primary care visit after the diagnosis</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Not repeated today, because the visit was taken up by the new diagnosis. This departs from the care plan. He reports no low mood; the PHQ-2 is due at the post-staging visit</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>CBC, basic metabolic panel, and albumin</td><td>Before and after treatment</td><td>Due</td><td>Baseline normal at intake; repeat before treatment starts, at the post-staging visit</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>TSH</td><td>Baseline before neck radiation, then every 6 to 12 months after it</td><td>Up to date</td><td>1.8 mIU/L at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Tobacco use status and cessation counseling</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No cigars for one week; counseling given</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Varenicline tolerance: nausea, sleep, mood, and behavior</td><td>Each visit during treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Nausea only when taken without food; no mood, sleep, or behavior change. Dose increased to 1 mg twice daily</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Tissue diagnosis within two weeks of the first visit. Outcome by 1884-07-21: Biopsy at the otolaryngology visit two weeks after presentation [S]</item><item>Stop all tobacco use before treatment begins. In progress; target 1884-08-04 [S]</item><item>Limit weight loss to less than 10% of baseline weight through treatment. In progress; target 1884-10-22 [S]</item><item>Keep throat pain at 4 or below on the 0-10 scale most days. In progress; target 1884-10-22 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: NCCN Guidelines Insights: Head and Neck Cancers, Version 2.2025 (2025); Tobacco Smoking Cessation in Adults, Including Pregnant Persons: Interventions (2021); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression and hypothyroidism monographs (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Telephone call with the final pathology report within a few days. PET/CT next week. Primary care visit after staging in about two weeks. Next scheduled visit 1884-08-04: primary care visit after staging to coordinate nutrition, dental care, tobacco cessation, and symptom control before treatment. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
